<title>GERMANY: Audi reviewing employee bonus programmes.</title>
<headline>Audi reviewing employee bonus programmes.</headline>
<dateline>INGOLSTADT, Germany 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>German luxury carmaker Audi AG, a unit of Volkswagen AG, said on Wednesday that it was reviewing programmes on how its employees could participate financially in the company's performance.</p>
<p>Audi management board member Andreas Schleef said at the carmaker's annual general meeting that possible programmes were under discussion that would reward employees based on Audi's sales, quality, productivity and number of sick days.</p>
<p>The carmaker was also reviewing the terms of a similar programme recently announced by Volkswagen for its employees.</p>
<p>Schleef did not say when any such programme would begin at Audi.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
